---
title: Supported Webhook Events
sidebar:
  order: 4
---
Taskip allows you to subscribe to a wide range of events so that your webhooks are triggered automatically whenever specific actions occur. By subscribing to these events, you can integrate Taskip with third-party applications, automate workflows, and receive real-time updates without manual monitoring.

These events are organized by category—such as support tickets, forms, sales pipelines, projects, invoices, meetings, and more—so you can choose exactly which actions should notify your webhook endpoint.

## **Events Supported By Webhook**

{% table %}
- Event Name
- Description
---
- support.ticket.created
- Triggered when a new support ticket is created.
---
- support.ticket.status.updated
- Triggered when a support ticket’s status changes.
---
- support.ticket.deleted
- Triggered when a support ticket is deleted.
{% /table %}

{% table %}
- Event Name
- Description
---
- form.created
- Triggered when a new form is created.
---
- form.submitted
- Triggered when a form is submitted by a user.
{% /table %}

{% table %}
- Event Name
- Description
---
- sales.pipeline.deal.created
- Triggered when a new deal is created in the sales pipeline.
---
- sales.pipeline.deal.stage.change
- Triggered when a deal moves to a different stage.
---
- sales.pipeline.deal.task.created
- Triggered when a task is created within a deal.
---
- sales.pipeline.deal.task.activity.created
- Triggered when a new activity is logged on a deal task.
---
- sales.pipeline.deal.task.meeting.created
- Triggered when a meeting is scheduled for a deal task.
{% /table %}

